\newlabel{tab:gaming}{{2}{11}{E7 --- the gaming gap at 20 probes/cell, mean over five families. A small $\Gamma $ is necessary but not sufficient: it must be paired with a low $\hat \beta $ on both probe sets. $^\dagger $Control foil}{table.caption.27}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{E6: a pipeline breach that no component explains.}{11}{section*.24}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{E7: a foil that passes public certification by detecting probes.}{11}{section*.25}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces E6/E7 --- the limits of certification. (a) Local certification does not compose: retriever A and orchestrator B each certify locally at $\hat  \beta =0$, but the interface carries the retriever secret $s_A$ into the orchestrator and the composed pipeline breaches at $\hat  \beta =1.0$ (20/20; Wilson [0.84, 1.00])---no component is individually non-compliant. (b) Public certification can be gamed: the probe-aware foil passes public certification and fails the held-out paraphrases ($\Gamma =1$); the two controls---a semantics-only foil that fails both and a resistant foil that passes both---show that a small $\Gamma $ is necessary but not sufficient: it must be paired with a low $\hat  \beta $ on both probe sets.}}{12}{figure.caption.26}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:limits}{{6}{12}{E6/E7 --- the limits of certification. (a) Local certification does not compose: retriever A and orchestrator B each certify locally at $\hat \beta =0$, but the interface carries the retriever secret $s_A$ into the orchestrator and the composed pipeline breaches at $\hat \beta =1.0$ (20/20; Wilson [0.84, 1.00])---no component is individually non-compliant. (b) Public certification can be gamed: the probe-aware foil passes public certification and fails the held-out paraphrases ($\Gamma =1$); the two controls---a semantics-only foil that fails both and a resistant foil that passes both---show that a small $\Gamma $ is necessary but not sufficient: it must be paired with a low $\hat \beta $ on both probe sets}{figure.caption.26}{}}
